<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-bg"></div>
  <div class="hero-content">
    <div class="hero-eyebrow">Franchise Opportunity</div>
    <h1>Own a <span>Pizza World</span> Franchise</h1>
    <p>Join America's most franchisee-friendly pizza company. Low startup costs, the industry's lowest royalty rate, and a gourmet product that keeps customers coming back. Since 1996.</p>
    <div class="hero-buttons">
      <a class="btn btn-red" href="#contact">Request Franchise Info</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="#investment">See the Numbers</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BY THE NUMBERS -->
<div class="numbers">
  <div class="numbers-grid">
    <div class="num-card"><div class="val">$43B</div><div class="lbl">Pizza Industry Size</div></div>
    <div class="num-card"><div class="val">2.75%</div><div class="lbl">Royalty — Industry's Lowest</div></div>
    <div class="num-card"><div class="val">29+</div><div class="lbl">Years in Business</div></div>
    <div class="num-card"><div class="val">12+</div><div class="lbl">Locations &amp; Growing</div></div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- WHY PIZZA WORLD -->
<section class="why" id="why">
  <span class="section-label">The Opportunity</span>
  <h2 class="section-title">Why <span>Pizza World?</span></h2>
  <p class="section-desc">Because it's all about your bottom line. We built Pizza World to be the most franchise-friendly brand in the industry. Low overhead. Premium product. Real support.</p>
  <div class="why-grid">
    <div class="why-img">
      <img src="https://mypizzaworld.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/DSC02136-43.jpg" alt="Pizza World Gourmet Pizza">
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:24px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:20px;">Built for <span style="color:var(--red);">Franchise Owners</span></h3>
      <ul class="checkmarks">
        <li>Standard store startup: $138K – $286K</li>
        <li>C-Store concept available from just $92K</li>
        <li>SBA Approved — bank financing available</li>
        <li>Only 2.75% royalty — the industry's lowest</li>
        <li>Virtual training program + 2 weeks hands-on at a live store</li>
        <li>Ongoing virtual training platform for all new employees</li>
        <li>Turnkey store package — we handle the buildout specs</li>
        <li>Proprietary POS system with online ordering built in</li>
        <li>Full marketing support — menus, postcards, social media toolkit</li>
        <li>Real gourmet product — 19+ specialty pizzas from around the world</li>
        <li>Simple operations — minimal waste, reasonable labor costs</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FOOD STRIP -->
<section class="food-strip" id="food">
  <span class="section-label">The Menu</span>
  <h2>More Than Just <span style="color:var(--red2);">Pizza</span></h2>
  <p>Salads, wings, subs, pasta, calzones, and more — a full menu that drives repeat business and higher average tickets.</p>
  <div class="food-scroll">
    <div class="food-card"><img src="img/pizza.jpg" alt="Gourmet Pizza"><div class="food-card-body"><h4>19 Gourmet Pizzas</h4></div></div>
    <div class="food-card"><img src="img/wings.jpg" alt="Wings"><div class="food-card-body"><h4>World Famous Wings</h4></div></div>
    <div class="food-card"><img src="img/subs.jpg" alt="Subs"><div class="food-card-body"><h4>Baked Fresh Subs</h4></div></div>
    <div class="food-card"><img src="img/salad.jpg" alt="Salads"><div class="food-card-body"><h4>Specialty Salads</h4></div></div>
    <div class="food-card"><img src="https://pizzaworldonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Canelloni.jpg" alt="Pasta"><div class="food-card-body"><h4>Baked Pasta</h4></div></div>
    <div class="food-card"><img src="https://pizzaworldonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/PW-Calzone-2-scaled-1.jpeg" alt="Calzones"><div class="food-card-body"><h4>Stuffed Calzones</h4></div></div>
    <div class="food-card"><img src="https://pizzaworldonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/DSC02609-130-scaled.jpg" alt="Desserts"><div class="food-card-body"><h4>Cinnamon Desserts</h4></div></div>
    <div class="food-card"><img src="https://pizzaworldonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/PW-Toasted-Raviola-1-scaled-1.jpeg" alt="Toasted Ravioli"><div class="food-card-body"><h4>Toasted Ravioli</h4></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INVESTMENT -->
<section class="investment" id="investment">
  <span class="section-label">The Investment</span>
  <h2 class="section-title" style="text-align:center;">What It <span>Costs</span></h2>
  <p class="section-desc" style="text-align:center;margin:0 auto;">Transparent pricing. No hidden fees. One of the most affordable franchise opportunities in the pizza industry.</p>
  <div class="invest-grid">
    <div class="invest-card">
      <div class="val">$19,500</div>
      <div class="lbl">Initial franchise fee — fully earned at signing. Development fee: $8,000/store for multi-unit deals</div>
    </div>
    <div class="invest-card">
      <div class="val">$138K–$286K</div>
      <div class="lbl">Total estimated startup — standard store including equipment, buildout, inventory &amp; working capital</div>
    </div>
    <div class="invest-card">
      <div class="val">$92K–$232K</div>
      <div class="lbl">C-Store concept — lower cost entry point with the same great Pizza World product</div>
    </div>
    <div class="invest-card">
      <div class="val">2.75%</div>
      <div class="lbl">Royalty on net sales — the lowest franchise royalty in the pizza industry</div>
    </div>
    <div class="invest-card">
      <div class="val">0%</div>
      <div class="lbl">We don’t take any marketing fees</div>
    </div>
    <div class="invest-card">
      <div class="val">10 + 10</div>
      <div class="lbl">Year franchise agreement term — 10 years initial, renewable for an additional 10 years</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- MARKETING SUPPORT -->
<section class="marketing" id="marketing">
  <div class="marketing-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="section-label">Franchise Support</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Franchise <span>Marketing Support</span><br><span>0% Marketing Fund</span></h2>
      <p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom:20px;"><strong style="color:var(--gold);">Professional Marketing Tools. Local Control.</strong></p>
      <p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom:20px;">Pizza World provides every franchise location with access to professionally designed marketing materials, including menus, postcards, flyers, coupons, in-store posters, window clings, box toppers, social media graphics, product photography, and more.</p>
      <p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom:20px;">Marketing efforts may include direct mail, digital advertising, social media, community events, sponsorships, local promotions, and other approved initiatives that help build awareness and drive sales.</p>
      <p class="section-desc">Every franchisee also receives access to our proprietary Marketing Hub—a centralized digital resource containing social media content, email templates, brand materials, promotional graphics, product photos, and other tools designed to make local marketing easier and more effective.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="marketing-img">
      <img src="img/franchise-marketing-hub.jpg" alt="Pizza World Marketing Hub">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TESTIMONIALS -->
<section class="testimonials" id="testimonials">
  <div style="text-align:center;">
    <span class="section-label">Success Stories</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Hear From Our <span>Franchise Owners</span></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="test-grid">
    <div class="test-card">
      <div class="test-quote">"I started as a store employee and worked my way up to owning my own franchise. Pizza World gave me the opportunity and the support to make it happen."</div>
      <div class="test-author">Bittney — Branson, MO</div>
    </div>
    <div class="test-card">
      <div class="test-quote">"My wife and I run our Pizza World together. It's been an incredible journey — we've built a successful business as a team, and the corporate support makes all the difference."</div>
      <div class="test-author">Duane — Indian Point, MO</div>
    </div>
    <div class="test-card">
      <div class="test-quote">"We looked for 15 years trying pizzas from Los Angeles to Virginia but kept coming back to Pizza World. The product is that good — and the franchise model made it a no-brainer."</div>
      <div class="test-author">Bob Jordan — Cedar Rapids, IA</div>
    </div>
    <div class="test-card">
      <div class="test-quote">"I’ve worked in the pizza industry for many years. When I decided to pursue my own pizza franchise, the Pizza World system just made sense. The superior products, low royalty rate, and 0% marketing fund — with all the marketing support I needed — made my choice easy."</div>
      <div class="test-author">John Hartman — Belleville, Illinois</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- LEADERSHIP TEAM -->
<section class="team" id="team" style="padding:90px 40px;max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;">
  <div style="text-align:center;">
    <span class="section-label">Leadership</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Who's <span>Behind Pizza World</span></h2>
    <p class="section-desc" style="text-align:center;margin:0 auto 40px;">A family-run business with decades of experience in operations, training, marketing, and franchise development.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:24px;">
    <div style="background:var(--dark2);border:1px solid #222;border-radius:10px;padding:30px;text-align:center;border-top:3px solid var(--red);">
      <div style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:20px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4px;">Eric P. Wortham</div>
      <div style="font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:14px;">Chairman, CEO &amp; President</div>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--gray);line-height:1.7;">Founder and architect of the Pizza World system. Developed the operating system, training manual, marketing manual, and turnkey store package. Business Administration background with emphasis on Marketing and Management.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--dark2);border:1px solid #222;border-radius:10px;padding:30px;text-align:center;border-top:3px solid var(--red);">
      <div style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:20px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4px;">Ryan Wortham</div>
      <div style="font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:14px;">VP &amp; Director of Operations &amp; Training</div>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--gray);line-height:1.7;">Leads all operations and training since 2015. Instrumental in new product development, directs training programs, and assists in every new store opening. Also owns his own Pizza World franchise — one of two training facilities.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section id="faq" style="padding:90px 40px;background:var(--dark2);">
  <div style="text-align:center;">
    <span class="section-label">Questions?</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Frequently <span>Asked Questions</span></h2>
  </div>
  <div style="max-width:800px;margin:40px auto 0;">
    <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #222;padding:20px 0;cursor:pointer;">
      <summary style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:16px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:#fff;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">What sets Pizza World apart? <span style="color:var(--red);font-size:20px;">+</span></summary>
      <p style="color:var(--gray);font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;margin-top:14px;">Pizza World combines the world's finest gourmet pizzas with subs, calzones, salads, wings and traditional pizzas — all available for quick delivery or dine-in. We use only the freshest ingredients, real cheese, homemade sauce, and freshly baked dough. The entire system is designed for simplicity and customer convenience. We're changing the way the world thinks about pizza.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #222;padding:20px 0;cursor:pointer;">
      <summary style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:16px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:#fff;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">What are the space requirements? <span style="color:var(--red);font-size:20px;">+</span></summary>
      <p style="color:var(--gray);font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;margin-top:14px;">Delivery-focused units require 1,100 to 1,300 sq ft. Delivery plus sit-down restaurant units can go up to 2,400 sq ft. Typically located in strip centers (in-line or end caps) with good signage visibility, strong traffic counts, and proximity to residential areas, schools, and other customer sources.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #222;padding:20px 0;cursor:pointer;">
      <summary style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:16px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:#fff;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">What training is provided? <span style="color:var(--red);font-size:20px;">+</span></summary>
      <p style="color:var(--gray);font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;margin-top:14px;">It starts with our virtual training program that franchisees complete before ever stepping into a store. Then two weeks of hands-on training at a designated Pizza World location covering operations, computer systems, food preparation, delivery, daily management, and more. The virtual training platform stays available after opening — every new employee you hire goes through it too. Plus you get in-store assistance during your grand opening and ongoing support.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #222;padding:20px 0;cursor:pointer;">
      <summary style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:16px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:#fff;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">How long does it take to open? <span style="color:var(--red);font-size:20px;">+</span></summary>
      <p style="color:var(--gray);font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;margin-top:14px;">Construction typically takes 90 to 120 days, depending on location, store style, and size. Pizza World provides site and plan approval, construction and equipment specifications, design specifications, and approved supplier lists to streamline the process.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #222;padding:20px 0;cursor:pointer;">
      <summary style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:16px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:#fff;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">Is financing available? <span style="color:var(--red);font-size:20px;">+</span></summary>
      <p style="color:var(--gray);font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;margin-top:14px;">Yes — Pizza World is SBA approved, which means qualified candidates can access Small Business Administration financing through participating banks. You must demonstrate the financial ability to start, build, and manage the business.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #222;padding:20px 0;cursor:pointer;">
      <summary style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:16px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:#fff;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">What ongoing fees are there? <span style="color:var(--red);font-size:20px;">+</span></summary>
